(7542635, 1207009, 28742, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2017-11-05 20:46:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542636, 1207290, 28742, '<td valign="top">You''ll probably get ding''d for overdoing the processing. I''m cool with it, though. It''s a nice scene and I like the brush strokes. If you added texture to the whole thing, it''s not that noticeable (a plus, IMO) because of the artistic filter(s) used. Good job.</td>', 'You''ll probably get ding''d for overdoing the processing. I''m cool with it, though. It''s a nice scene and I like the brush strokes. If you added texture to the whole thing, it''s not that noticeable (a plus, IMO) because of the artistic filter(s) used. Good job.', '2017-11-05 20:49:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542637, 1207402, 28742, '<td valign="top">Oddly enough, I want to bash this a little for being seemingly mundane and/or lacking a decent subject, but the more I look, the more I like. So... 8 from me.</td>', 'Oddly enough, I want to bash this a little for being seemingly mundane and/or lacking a decent subject, but the more I look, the more I like. So... 8 from me.', '2017-11-05 20:51:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542638, 1207414, 173844, '<td valign="top">Very appealing scene, in which you feel as if you''ve stepped into a breeze.  The colors are harmonious with the season, and the mood is gentle.  What I don''t understand in the context of a painting is the focus.  We are used to seeing part of a photograph in focus, here the tree leaves, with the rest of the scene being not being in focus, to the point of becoming bokeh.  In paintings, however, and I might be wrong about this, this phenomenon is rarely present.  The focus, if anything, fades out very little and very gradually.  So in this particular instant, the photograph doesn''t convincingly translate to a painterly version.  I''m belaboring the issue because I otherwise like the image.</td>', 'Very appealing scene, in which you feel as if you''ve stepped into a breeze.  The colors are harmonious with the season, and the mood is gentle.  What I don''t understand in the context of a painting is the focus.  We are used to seeing part of a photograph in focus, here the tree leaves, with the rest of the scene being not being in focus, to the point of becoming bokeh.  In paintings, however, and I might be wrong about this, this phenomenon is rarely present.  The focus, if anything, fades out very little and very gradually.  So in this particular instant, the photograph doesn''t convincingly translate to a painterly version.  I''m belaboring the issue because I otherwise like the image.', '2017-11-05 20:53:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542639, 1207357, 28742, '<td valign="top">Spectacular shot! I hope you''ll post the original after the challenge. Would like to see if the "painterly" processing hurt this or helped it. 9 from me.</td>', 'Spectacular shot! I hope you''ll post the original after the challenge. Would like to see if the "painterly" processing hurt this or helped it. 9 from me.', '2017-11-05 20:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542640, 1207097, 28742, '<td valign="top">Boy, I really don''t want to bitch about the grass and the sky, but I feel like you went a little too far on those in what seems to me would have otherwise been my very top pick. Would love to see the original.</td>', 'Boy, I really don''t want to bitch about the grass and the sky, but I feel like you went a little too far on those in what seems to me would have otherwise been my very top pick. Would love to see the original.', '2017-11-05 20:56:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542641, 1207239, 28742, '<td valign="top">Stunning! Only nitpick is that you all but wisped away the boat completely out of the scene. A lighter touch on that would''ve helped with my score anyway. 7</td>', 'Stunning! Only nitpick is that you all but wisped away the boat completely out of the scene. A lighter touch on that would''ve helped with my score anyway. 7', '2017-11-05 20:58:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542642, 1207270, 28742, '<td valign="top">Saturation level 9000. ;-) A great scene, but maybe too harsh on the color sat.</td>', 'Saturation level 9000. ;-) A great scene, but maybe too harsh on the color sat.', '2017-11-05 20:59:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542643, 1207421, 28742, '<td valign="top">Only issue with this beautiful scene is maybe the composition. I might like it better with the left side cropped out more, uncentering the bridge. Great job, though.</td>', 'Only issue with this beautiful scene is maybe the composition. I might like it better with the left side cropped out more, uncentering the bridge. Great job, though.', '2017-11-05 21:00:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542644, 1207362, 28742, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous dog, great scene. Processing just isn''t working for me. Not so much a painterly feel as smudged or blurred. Worth a 6 with a potential revisit and bump.</td>', 'Gorgeous dog, great scene. Processing just isn''t working for me. Not so much a painterly feel as smudged or blurred. Worth a 6 with a potential revisit and bump.', '2017-11-05 21:02:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542645, 1207095, 173844, '<td valign="top">Though the trees and foreground are fairly dark, this merely serves to heighten the bright sunshine of the green field.  We have a copse-eye view of the world beyond, an intriguingly unique vision.  The mood is both bright and a bit ominous.  I like the effect very much.  The painterly treatment is subtle and enhances the overall tone.  I like the dead leaves scattered across the lower left corner -- their realism draws you into the scene and is a transition to the inviting glow of the copse and field.</td>', 'Though the trees and foreground are fairly dark, this merely serves to heighten the bright sunshine of the green field.  We have a copse-eye view of the world beyond, an intriguingly unique vision.  The mood is both bright and a bit ominous.  I like the effect very much.  The painterly treatment is subtle and enhances the overall tone.  I like the dead leaves scattered across the lower left corner -- their realism draws you into the scene and is a transition to the inviting glow of the copse and field.', '2017-11-05 21:04:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542646, 1207048, 28742, '<td valign="top">Doesn''t really seem like you added any painterly processing to this. ...congratulations! :) It seems you nailed it without cheap tricks or gimmicks - none of which I am opposed to or dislike, btw. If you did use anything, you did it masterfully. 10</td>', 'Doesn''t really seem like you added any painterly processing to this. ...congratulations! :) It seems you nailed it without cheap tricks or gimmicks - none of which I am opposed to or dislike, btw. If you did use anything, you did it masterfully. 10', '2017-11-05 21:04:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542647, 1207147, 28742, '<td valign="top">Yeah, I could see this hanging on the wall at my therapists office. ;-)</td>', 'Yeah, I could see this hanging on the wall at my therapists office. ;-)', '2017-11-05 21:05:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7542648, 1207274, 28742, '<td valign="top">I really want to like this more. Maybe I''m having a problem with the white at the bottom that may be snow, but appears to look more like foam which isn''t pleasant to look at in a pond or lake. I think a crop off of ~10% of the top and bottom might have made this better. A solid 6 with a potential bump if it calls me back. :)</td>', 'I really want to like this more. Maybe I''m having a problem with the white at the bottom that may be snow, but appears to look more like foam which isn''t pleasant to look at in a pond or lake. I think a crop off of ~10% of the top and bottom might have made this better. A solid 6 with a potential bump if it calls me back. :)', '2017-11-05 21:09:16.000000', NULL, 1),
